<p>The U.S. House of Representatives voted on April 16 to block the Trump administration from ending temporary deportation protections for Haitians living in the United States, with all House Democrats and four Republicans backing the measure. The vote would preserve Temporary Protected Status for more than 300,000 Haitians, with some reports putting the figure at about 350,000, in a rare House rebuke of President Trump&#x27;s immigration agenda. The decision focuses on conditions in Haiti and the legal status of Haitians already living in the U.S., not on creating a new immigration program. For affected families, the vote offers some short-term stability and shows that a measure of bipartisan support emerged, even if limited, for keeping protections in place while the broader policy fight continues.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Procedural significance: CBS reports that supporters forced a House vote on the measure, turning Haitian TPS into a direct floor test.</li><li>Symbolic weight: Reuters-based reports describe the vote as an unusual House challenge to President Trump&#x27;s immigration enforcement agenda, giving even a small Republican crossover real political significance.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>House Democrats: Democrats backed the measure unanimously, helping force a vote and pass protections that keep Haitian deportation relief in place. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/house-vote-haiti-tps-trump-deportation-protections-trump-immigration/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Republican supporters: Four Republicans broke with President Trump and voted with Democrats, signaling limited bipartisan concern about ending the protections. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-house-votes-to-defy-trump-extend-haitians-temporary-protections'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: The administration moved to end Haitians&#x27; temporary deportation protections as part of President Trump&#x27;s broader immigration enforcement agenda. (<a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/us-house-votes-to-defy-trump-extend-haitians%27-temporary-protections2'>Japan Today</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/house-vote-haiti-tps-trump-deportation-protections-trump-immigration/'>House breaks with Trump, votes against ending deportation protections for Haitians</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-house-votes-to-defy-trump-extend-haitians-temporary-protections'>US House votes to defy Trump, extend Haitians&#x27; temporary protections</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1sne3y5/house_passes_a_bill_to_protect_haitian_immigrants/'>House passes a bill to protect Haitian immigrants, in slap back to the Trump administration</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/us-house-votes-to-defy-trump-extend-haitians%27-temporary-protections2'>U.S. House votes to defy Trump; extend Haitians&#x27; temporary protections</a> - japantoday.com</li></ul>